

             Readme Notes for 4D-BBS V2.92  December 31, 1993
             ------------------------------------------------


This version now includes a new installer script.  The installer script
requires the source of the installation to be from a path called
"4D-BBS_Install:".  This means either the floppy must be named
"4D-BBS_Install" or you need to assign 4D-BBS_Install: to the directory
where the installation source files and directories may be found are found.

If you do no have the Commodore Installer program, you will need to either
copy it from another software package which does have it or download it
from a BBS (it is on the CornerStone Software support BBS).  If the
Installer program is not in your path, highlight the install icon, and use
information from Workbench to change the path of the default tooltype to
point to where Installer is located at on your system.

The default setup uses a couple of assigns.  Namely these are File:, Text:,
and Boards:.  YOU WILL NEED TO MAKE THESE ASSIGNS BEFORE RUNNING THE BBS OR
YOU WILL GET A REQUESTOR WHEN USING SOME PARTS OF THE BBS.  To avoid this
run b_ed and fcl_ed and change the paths of the default sections to point
to where you wish the files for each section to be stored.  The Text:
assign is in several of the menus, and you will need to change them to an
explicit path if you wish to get rid of the text:  assign.  It is normally
easier to just add an assign for it in your S:User-Startup or the StartBBS
script.

